# Copy to .env (gitignored; Bun loads it). The dev shell sets DATABASE_URL and PUBLIC_ORIGIN.
#
# Sign-in providers: each is off unless both its variables are set. Register each OAuth app with the
# callback URL <PUBLIC_ORIGIN>/api/auth/<provider>/callback, e.g. http://localhost:4202/api/auth/github/callback
# for workspace ws2.
#
# GitHub: https://github.com/settings/developers
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# Discord: https://discord.com/developers/applications (OAuth2 redirects)
# DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=
# DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# Google: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials (OAuth client ID, web application)
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# docker compose (docs/deployment.md). POSTGRES_PASSWORD is required there; pick a long random value, e.g.
# `openssl rand -hex 24`, and single-quote it if it contains `$`. PIONEER_PORT is the host port (default 8080).
# Set PUBLIC_ORIGIN to the address browsers use when it is not http://localhost:<PIONEER_PORT>.
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# PIONEER_PORT=8080
